# Bounded-execution scratch. qta_agent/execution.py makes one of these per
# run with tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=".exec-", dir=cwd) and removes it in its
# `finally` -- it holds a child process's stdout and stderr while the run is
# in flight and is never work product. A process that dies before that
# `finally` (SIGKILL, a killed test session) leaks one, and because
# generate_manifest.py refuses any path that is untracked and not ignored,
# an unrelated crash then reports MANIFEST DRIFT. Observed in this
# repository, on a test session killed mid-run.
.exec-*/
